msgstr ""

msgid "**Access log class:** the reverse proxy writes its access log to stdout and its error log to stderr, and Docker's journald driver stores a container's stdout lines at journal priority 6 and its stderr lines at priority 3. A line of an application in `LOG_COLLECTOR_ACCESS_LOG_APPLICATIONS` (`svc-prx-openresty`) at priority 6 is therefore classed `access`, while the proxy's error log stays `application`. The critical-line alerts of Loki and Grafana select `log_class=\"application\"` only, so an access log line no longer raises them. The proxy's error log still does: a request it logs as an error, such as a missing file under the CDN location (`open() \"<path>\" failed`), carries the request path into an `application` line, and an alert word in that path raises both alerts."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Access log class:** the reverse proxy writes its access log to stdout and its error log to stderr, and Docker’s journald driver stores a container’s stdout lines at journal priority 6 and its stderr lines at priority 3. A line of an application in ``LOG_COLLECTOR_ACCESS_LOG_APPLICATIONS`` (``svc-prx-openresty``) at priority 6 is therefore classed ``access``, while the proxy’s error log stays ``application``. The critical-line alerts of Loki and Grafana select ``log_class=\"application\"`` only, so an access log line no longer raises them. The proxy’s error log still does: a request it logs as an error, such as a missing file under the CDN location (``open() \"<path>\" failed``), carries the request path into an ``application`` line, and an alert word in that path raises both alerts."
msgstr ""

