msgid "**Admin Flag From RBAC:** [files/python/rbac_sync.py](./files/python/rbac_sync.py) sets the Pixelfed admin flag on the members of the `administrator` role group, matched by username, e-mail or OIDC mapping, and clears it on every other account. It runs as a host hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) against the database container at every deploy and on its timer. With `sso`, the listener [files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php](./files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php), mounted into `app/Listeners` where Laravel's event discovery registers it, applies the same flag at every OIDC sign-in from the `administrator` group in the groups claim, which [files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php](./files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php) reads off the userinfo response on its way through `UserOidcService`; a group change therefore reaches the account at its next sign-in, and a new member holds the flag from its first one. The administrator created through artisan keeps the flag."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag From RBAC:** `files/python/rbac_sync.py <./files/python/rbac_sync.py>`__ sets the Pixelfed admin flag on the members of the ``administrator`` role group, matched by username, e-mail or OIDC mapping, and clears it on every other account. It runs as a host hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ against the database container at every deploy and on its timer. With ``sso``, the listener `files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php <./files/php/rbac/oidc_login.php>`__, mounted into ``app/Listeners`` where Laravel’s event discovery registers it, applies the same flag at every OIDC sign-in from the ``administrator`` group in the groups claim, which `files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php <./files/php/rbac/userinfo_client.php>`__ reads off the userinfo response on its way through ``UserOidcService``; a group change therefore reaches the account at its next sign-in, and a new member holds the flag from its first one. The administrator created through artisan keeps the flag."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Admin Flag and Profile at Every SAML Sign-In:** the same extension sets ``is_admin`` from the ``administrator`` group and writes first and last name, work and mobile phone, title, department and address from the assertion (``SUITECRM_SAML_PROFILE_COLUMNS`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) into the user record."
