msgid "**Isolation contract:** ``services.workspace.isolation`` encodes no host home, no sibling repositories, no host Docker socket, no host credentials, own-stack-only Docker access, unprivileged nested Docker with a refused privileged fallback, an uplink-pinned nested MTU, an approval store kept off the agent’s writable paths, and agent-firewall egress."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Isolation contract:** `services.workspace.isolation` encodes no host home, no sibling repositories, no host Docker socket, no host credentials, own-stack-only Docker access, unprivileged nested Docker with a refused privileged fallback, an uplink-pinned nested MTU, an approval store kept off the agent's writable paths, and agent-firewall egress."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Isolation is gVisor on top of in-app sandboxing; Firecracker is out of reach on this engine.** Each agent app runs under `runtime: runsc`, a userspace guest kernel that intercepts syscalls before they reach the host, so untrusted model-generated code stays kernel-isolated even if the app's own sandbox is bypassed. No custom VMM, jailer wiring, or bespoke rootfs pipeline. E2B/Beam noted as alternatives in the role README but not adopted."
msgstr "**Izoliacija yra gVisor ant in- app smėlio bokso viršuje; Firecracker yra nepasiekiama šio variklio.** Kiekvienas agentas app veikia pagal `runtime: runsc`, userspace svečias branduolis, kad perima syscall prieš jie pasiekia priimančiosios, todėl nepatikimas modelis sukurtas kodas lieka izoliuotas, net jei programa savo smėlio dėžutė yra aplenktas. Nėra užsakymą VMM, jailer laidų, arba bespoke rootfs vamzdynas. E2B / Beam pažymėjo, kaip alternatyva vaidmens README, bet nepriimtas."

msgid "**Isolation:** Every agent runs in its own container or single-replica service under the isolating runtime, with its own volume, its own network whose only other member is the broker, and its own bearer key; an agent that would start under ``runc`` is stopped and refused. In compose that network is created per agent and the broker attaches to it; in swarm, where a service task cannot be attached to a network it was not created with, the networks are a pool of ``agents.max_running`` overlays that the broker joins through its own service spec and each agent claims one of while it runs."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Isolation:** Every agent runs in its own container or single-replica service under the isolating runtime, with its own volume, its own network whose only other member is the broker, and its own bearer key; an agent that would start under `runc` is stopped and refused. In compose that network is created per agent and the broker attaches to it; in swarm, where a service task cannot be attached to a network it was not created with, the networks are a pool of `agents.max_running` overlays that the broker joins through its own service spec and each agent claims one of while it runs."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-format
msgid "**It is part of a row's identity.** The glyph is in the job label, the value in the artifact name, the column in the plan table, and `:arm64` narrows a selection token the way `%distro` and `/filesystem` do. A retrigger replays it, unlike the filesystem: the title states the machine the job actually ran on, not a preference it could have fallen back from."
msgstr "**Tai eilutės tapatybės dalis.** Glyph yra darbo etiketės, į artifacture pavadinimas vertė, plano lentelės stulpelis, ir `:arm64` susiaurina pažymėtą kelią `%distro` ir `/filesystem` Taip. Regaiduktas jį atkartoja, kitaip nei failų sistema: pavadinime nurodoma mašina, kurios darbas iš tikrųjų vyko, o ne pirmenybė, nuo kurios jis galėjo atsitraukti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**It rotates on the row's position directly, not as a third odometer digit.** The distro/filesystem odometer exists because two pools of equal length walked on the same index cover only `n` of `n x m` pairs. Two architectures against five distros are coprime, and against the fifteen distro/filesystem positions too, so the fast rotation reaches every pairing anyway. Making it the slowest digit would be actively wrong: a role with four rows would sit on one architecture forever, and the axis exists precisely so a role's own variants split over both."
msgstr "**Jis suka eilutės padėtyje tiesiogiai, ne kaip trečias odometro skaitmuo.** Disko / filesystem odometras egzistuoja todėl, kad du vienodo ilgio baseinai vaikščiojo tik ant to paties indekso viršelio `n` iš `n x m` poros. Dvi architektūros prieš penkis distronus yra koprimas, ir prieš penkiolika distrono / filesystem padėčių taip pat, todėl greitas rotacija pasiekia kiekvieną lyną vistiek. Padaryti jį lėčiausias skaitmuo būtų aktyviai negerai: vaidmuo su keturiomis eilėmis sėdėti ant vienos architektūros amžinai, ir ašis egzistuoja tiksliai, todėl vaidmuo savo variantus padalinti per abu."

msgid "**Iteration loop.** The agent MUST follow the [Compose Loop](../../agents/skills/i8-iterate-compose/SKILL.md) for every change inside `roles/svc-swarm-node/`, `roles/svc-prx-openresty/` (swarm-mode adaptations), `roles/svc-storage-nfs-server/`, `roles/svc-storage-nfs-client/`, and `roles/web-app-mediawiki/` (pilot). The agent MUST follow the [Workflow Loop](../../agents/skills/i8-iterate-workflow/SKILL.md) for every change to `.github/workflows/test-deploy-swarm-nfs.yml`. The agent MUST NOT skip the loop's debug-locally step in favour of remote CI reruns."
msgstr ""

