o an account a failed deploy created but never linked is linked on the next run while an account someone registered and logged into is never taken over, and `files/sql/rbac/reconcile-roles.sql <./files/sql/rbac/reconcile-roles.sql>`__ converges the PeerTube role of every OpenID Connect account to Administrator, Moderator or User from its groups. The same statement deletes every password-grant token of an OpenID Connect account: PeerTube refuses password logins to those, so such a token only stems from a login that read the account just before the link committed. A member added between deploys therefore has its role within one timer interval once the account exists, and gets a pre-provisioned account at the next deploy or its own at the first OIDC login. The local ``root`` account keeps its role, and its password never reaches the hook."
