msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows JavaScript to substitute a value for an unset environment variable. Reserved for a value the code itself owns and no role renders. Normalising to `\"\"`, `\"[]\"`, `false`, `0` or another `process.env` entry needs no marker."
msgstr "Leidžia JavaScript pakeisti nenustatyto aplinkos kintamojo vertę. Rezervuota vertei, kuri priklauso pačiam kodui ir neatlieka jokio vaidmens. Normalizavimas `\"\"`, `\"[]\"`, `false`, `0` arba kita `process.env` atvykimo nereikia žymeklis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows `*_CONTAINER_ADDRESS | quote` in a role task file. Reserved for sites that never see the swarm `$(...)` fragment (`IS_COMPOSE_MODE`-gated tasks, `compose_mode_force` roles) or consumers that re-evaluate the argument themselves."
msgstr "Leidžia `*_CONTAINER_ADDRESS | quote` į vaidmenį užduotį failą. Rezervuota toms vietoms, kurios niekada nemato sūpynės `$(...)` fragmentas (`IS_COMPOSE_MODE`- užduotys, `compose_mode_force` vaidmenys) arba vartotojams, kurie patys iš naujo įvertina argumentą."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows `... | bool == True/False/true/false` when a real tri-state guard is intended (distinguishing `None` from `False`)."
msgstr "Leidžia `... | bool == True/False/true/false` kai tikrasis trivalstijos sargybinis yra skirtas (skiriamasis `None` nuo `False`)."

msgid "Allows a Jinja expression to stand as a mapping key under `roles/*/meta/` or `roles/*/vars/`. Ansible renders the values of a loaded variable structure and leaves the keys as written, so the consumer receives the source text. Marker goes on or directly above the line."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `*.sh.j2` to exist. Default path: ship the script as a plain `.sh` under `files/shell/` and pass its values as `ExecStart` arguments or `Environment=` entries, because shellcheck, the repository's `.sh` guards and every test skip a Jinja template, so nothing reads what actually runs on the host. Reserved for a script whose shape is generated, not just its values. Place the marker BELOW the shebang, never above it, and prefer the Jinja comment form so it does not reach the rendered script."
msgstr "Leidžia `*.sh.j2` egzistuoti. Numatytasis kelias: rodyti scenarijų kaip paprastą `.sh` pagal `files/shell/` ir išlaikyti savo vertes kaip `ExecStart` argumentai arba `Environment=` įrašai, nes shellcheck, saugykla `.sh` sargybiniai ir kiekvienas bandymas praleisti Jinja šabloną, todėl niekas skaito, kas iš tikrųjų veikia ant šeimininko. Rezervuota scenarijui, kurio forma generuojama, ne tik jo reikšmes. Vieta žymeklis BELOW Šebang, niekada virš jo, ir pirmenybę Jinja komentarą forma, todėl ji nepasiekia lydytas scenarijų."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `.j2` template to write the software's name, domain or URL as a literal. Default path: render `SOFTWARE_NAME`, `SOFTWARE_DOMAIN`, `SOFTWARE_URL` or `ORGANIZATION`, which `group_vars/all/00_general.yml` declares once and derives from each other, so a rename reaches the template too. Reserved for a literal that must survive a rename, such as an identifier a third party issued under the old name."
msgstr "Leidžia `.j2` šabloną, kaip pažodinį, rašyti programinės įrangos pavadinimą, domeną ar URL. Numatytasis kelias: realizavimas `SOFTWARE_NAME`, `SOFTWARE_DOMAIN`, `SOFTWARE_URL` arba `ORGANIZATION`, `group_vars/all/00_general.yml` deklaruoja vieną kartą ir kilęs iš vienas kito, todėl pervadinti pasiekia šabloną per. Rezervuota pažodžiui, kuris turi išgyventi pervardą, pavyzdžiui, identifikatorių, kurį trečioji šalis išdavė pagal seną vardą."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `.py` file to carry a literal role-file path instead of the matching `ROLE_FILE_*` constant from `utils.roles.mapping`. Reserved for tests asserting the constant's value, migration scripts, or doc strings."
msgstr "Leidžia `.py` failą atlikti pažodinį role- failo kelią vietoj atitikimo `ROLE_FILE_*` pastovus nuo `utils.roles.mapping`. Rezervuota bandymams, patvirtinantiems konstantos vertę, migracijos scenarijus, arba doc stygos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `container exec` / `container inspect` target that does not route through the `container_address` lookup. Reserved for a container ID already resolved at `delegate_to` runtime (`*_LOCAL_CID`), where the lookup would return a manager-only subshell, and for deliberate bare-name partner probes gated on compose co-location."
msgstr "Leidžia `container exec` / `container inspect` per `container_address` Žiūrovai. Rezervuota konteinerio ID jau išspręstam `delegate_to` laikas (`*_LOCAL_CID`), kur peržiūros būtų grąžinti valdymo tik subshell, ir už sąmoningas Bare-name partnerio zondai priklijuotas ant formavimo ko- vieta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `container_address`-derived target to be reached from a `command: argv:` list, which runs no shell to evaluate the swarm `$(...)` fragment. Reserved for roles pinned to compose via `compose_mode_force`, where the lookup can only ever yield a bare name."
msgstr "Leidžia `container_address`Išvestinis tikslas turi būti pasiektas iš `command: argv:` sąrašas, kuris veikia be apvalkalo įvertinti pelkių `$(...)` fragmentas. Rezervuota tam, kad vaidmenys būtų sukurti per `compose_mode_force`, kur peržiūra gali duoti tik pliką vardą."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `loop_var` to take the name of a variable declared in `group_vars/**` or in a role's `vars`/`defaults`. Inside the loop that name carries the item, so every lookup, template and nested include reading it sees the item instead, and ansible only warns. Reserved for a loop whose body reads the name as the item on purpose, typically because the item IS that value: state which meaning the body relies on."
msgstr "Leidžia `loop_var` priimti kintamojo, deklaruoto `group_vars/**` arba `vars`/`defaults`. Viduje kilpos, kad pavadinimas atlieka elementą, todėl kiekvienas žvilgsnis, šablonas ir stested įtraukti skaityti ji mato elementą vietoj, ir tariamas tik įspėja. Rezervuota kilpai, kurios kūnas skaito pavadinimą kaip objekto paskirtį, paprastai dėl to, kad elementas IS, kad vertė: valstybė, kuria reiškia įstaiga remiasi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` `min_storage` to exceed the measured compressed size of its own `image:`/`version:` by more than 1 GB. MUST be paired with a `Reason:` on the same comment line naming what occupies the space. Reserved for services whose data volume genuinely dominates the footprint; the default path is to lower the value, because an over-declared budget makes a host look too small and prunes a cache the deploy did not need to lose."
msgstr "Leidžia `roles/*/meta/services.yml` `min_storage` viršyti išmatuotą suspaustą dydį savo `image:`/`version:` daugiau kaip 1 GB. PRIVALO būti poruojamas su `Reason:` toje pačioje komentaro eilutėje, pavadinant, kas užima erdvę. Rezervuota paslaugoms, kurių duomenų apimtis iš tikrųjų dominuoja; numatytasis kelias yra sumažinti vertę, nes per didelis deklaruotas biudžetas daro šeimininką atrodo per mažas ir slysta talpyklos dislokavimo nereikia prarasti."

msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` entity to declare `architectures`, which takes the role's rows out of part of the deploy matrix so it stops being exercised where it is narrowed away. MUST be paired with a `Reason:` naming what cannot run elsewhere. Reserved for an upstream that publishes no manifest for the dropped architecture; where the role builds its own image, the default path is to build it for both instead. [test_image_architectures.py](../../../../tests/external/update/docker/test_image_architectures.py) fails once every image the role pins publishes the narrowed-away architecture, which is when the declaration and this marker are deleted together."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` entry whose image declares a `VOLUME` the role mounts nothing at. MUST be paired with a `Reason:` naming the path and why the volume stays anonymous. Default path: declare the mount in `roles/<role>/meta/volumes.yml` against the service key the compose file names, because docker creates an anonymous volume for an unmounted `VOLUME` and `sys-ctl-hlth-volumes` fails the deploy over it — and its whitelist keys on volume ids, which are new on every deploy, so the gap cannot be suppressed there. Reserved for an anonymous volume that is genuinely intended: a scratch path the container rewrites on every start, whose contents no restore has to bring back."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` entry whose image ships no `HEALTHCHECK` to declare none either. Default path: add `healthcheck:` to the entry, because a container without a probe counts as healthy the moment its process starts — which is how a service that came back empty passes a restore drill. Reserved for containers nothing can probe: a one-shot process that exits, or an image with neither a port nor a shell."
msgstr "Leidžia `roles/*/meta/services.yml` įrašas, kurio atvaizdo laivai `HEALTHCHECK` taip pat neskelbti. Numatytas kelias: pridėti `healthcheck:` į įrašą, nes konteineris be zondo skaičiuoja kaip sveikas momentas jos procesas prasideda - kaip paslauga, kuri grįžo tuščia eina atkurti grąžtą. Rezervuota konteineriams niekas negali zondas: vieno šūvio procesas, kad išeina, arba vaizdas nei uosto, nei korpuso."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` `services.<key>` entry to reference a service key that is NOT declared as a top-level entry in `meta/services.yml`. Reserved for resolver-only matrix hooks (typically on invokable infrastructure roles) whose variant entries pin the round's companion topology via service-key flags the resolver maps to provider roles, with no real consumer contract in the base meta."
msgstr "Leidžia `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` `services.<key>` paslaugų rakto, kuris NEdeklaruojamas kaip viršutinio lygio įrašas, įrašas `meta/services.yml`. Skirta tik matricos kabliams (paprastai naudojantis infrastruktūros funkcijomis) kurio variantas įrašai prisegti turo kompanionas topologija per service- raktų vėliavos resolver žemėlapiai teikėjo vaidmenis, be nekilnojamojo vartotojo sutartis bazės meta."

msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` entry that pins `services.tor.enabled: false` to keep onion-capable frontend partners enabled. Place on the variant's own `tor` key line. The marker MUST name why those partners belong in a clearnet round; the usual reason is a real-time media partner in the same round whose transport the onion breaks."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` leaf override of an attribute whose base value in `meta/services.yml` is a static literal. Place on the override line in `variants.yml`. Use only when the consumer chain is provably immune to the variant-merge propagation gap; the default is to make the base value dynamic via `\"{{ '<role>' in group_names }}\"`."
msgstr "Leidžia `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` lapų nepaisyti požymio, kurio pagrindinė vertė `meta/services.yml` yra statinis pažodinis. Įdėti ant override linijos `variants.yml`. Naudoti tik tada, kai vartotojų grandinė yra akivaizdžiai atsparus variant- sujungti skleidimo spragą; numatytasis yra padaryti bazinės vertės dinamišką per `\"{{ '<role>' in group_names }}\"`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `services.<key>.healthcheck` that no `lookup('container_healthcheck', …)` call renders. Default path: add the lookup to the service block, because an unrendered declaration reads like the service is watched while the compose file carries no probe. Reserved for a call the static resolver cannot attribute — mastodon renders every service through a macro whose `service_name` is a macro parameter."
msgstr "Leidžia `services.<key>.healthcheck` kad ne `lookup('container_healthcheck', …)` Skambink. Numatytasis kelias: pridėti peržiūros į paslaugų bloką, nes nevirsta deklaracija skaito kaip paslauga yra žiūrima, o komponavimo failas neturi zondo. Rezervuota kvietimui Statinis resolver negali priskirti - mastodon teikia kiekvieną paslaugą per makro `service_name` yra makroparametras."

msgid "Allows a `test.skip(...)` or `test.fixme(...)` in `roles/*/files/playwright/**/*.js` whose condition reads an `sso`, `ldap` or `oidc` value, directly, through a binding in the role's Playwright directory, or as the `if` around an unconditional skip. Default path: `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(\"<svc>\")` or `skipUnlessServiceDisabled(\"<svc>\")` from `./service-gating`, followed by `expect(...)` for every value the enabled service must render. Reserved for a gate on something that is not the service itself, such as a flavor or a plugin capability inside a canonical service gate. Write it as `// nocheck: playwright-sso-ldap-gate -- <reason>`; a reason shorter than ten characters grants nothing."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a bare curl invocation without the `curl` filter or inline `--max-time`."
msgstr "Leidžia plika garbanos užpuolimą be `curl` filtras arba inline `--max-time`."

msgid "Allows a bridged `roles/*/meta/addons/*.yml` addon that is required or enabled by default without naming `services.<target>.enabled` for every bridge. The reason is mandatory. Default path: gate `enabled` on every bridged partner, joined with `or` when any one suffices."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a conditional `resolve_host_cid` include whose `<PREFIX>_HOST_NODE` a `delegate_to` in the same role reads. Marker goes on or directly above the include's `- name:`."
msgstr "Leidžia sąlyginį `resolve_host_cid` įskaitant `<PREFIX>_HOST_NODE` a `delegate_to` tuo pačiu vaidmuo skamba. Žymeklis tęsiasi arba tiesiai virš įtraukti `- name:`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a file to contain its own relative path from the repo root as a string literal. Reserved for load-bearing self-references. Repo-root files are exempt without a marker."
msgstr "Leidžia failą, kad būtų savo santykinį kelią nuo atpirkimo šaknų kaip styginių pažodinis. Skirta savivarčiams. Atgaminti šakninius failus yra atleidžiami be žymeklio."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a hardcoded `http://` / `https://` literal next to a `lookup(...)` call. Reserved for genuinely fixed protocols (Docker-network upstreams, loopback URLs in CI fixtures)."
msgstr "Leidžia užkoduoti `http://` / `https://` pažodžiui šalia `lookup(...)` Skambink. Rezervuota tikrai fiksuotiems protokolams (Dokumentų tinklo upuuflows, locback URL CI įrenginiai)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a lookup plugin (`plugins/lookup/` or `roles/*/lookup_plugins/`) to import a config-merge function from `utils.cache.applications` / `.domains` / `.users` instead of reaching the SPOT via `lookup_loader.get('applications'/'config'/'domains'/'users')`. Reserved for the SPOT providers (`applications` / `config` / `applications_current_play` / `users` / `domains`) and the raw-volume accessors (`volume` / `nginx`)."
msgstr "Leidžia peržiūrėti įskiepį (`plugins/lookup/` arba `roles/*/lookup_plugins/`) Importuoti konfigūravimo sujungimo funkciją iš `utils.cache.applications` / `.domains` / `.users` Vietoj to, kad pasiekti SPOT per `lookup_loader.get('applications'/'config'/'domains'/'users')`. Rezervuota SPOT tiekėjų (`applications` / `config` / `applications_current_play` / `users` / `domains`) ir sūkuriniai priedai (`volume` / `nginx`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `Path.read_text` / `Path.read_bytes` call in `tests/lint/` outside the LRU-cached `utils.cache.files.read_text` contract."
msgstr "Leidžia žalią `Path.read_text` / `Path.read_bytes` skambutis `tests/lint/` ne LRU- cached `utils.cache.files.read_text` sutartis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `Path.rglob`, `os.walk`, or `glob.glob` call outside the `utils.cache.files.iter_project_files` contract."
msgstr "Leidžia žalią `Path.rglob`, `os.walk`, arba `glob.glob` Skambinkite ne į `utils.cache.files.iter_project_files` sutartis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `container_name:` key in a `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` template. Default path: route through the generic `compose_only` lookup (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'container_name', NAME) }}`) so swarm-mode replicas do not collide on the static name."
msgstr "Leidžia žalią `container_name:` raktas `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` šabloną. Numatytasis kelias: maršrutas per bendrinį `compose_only` paieška (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'container_name', NAME) }}`) taip sūkurinių režimas replikos nesusiduria su statinio pavadinimo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `pull_policy:` key in a `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` template. Default path: route through the generic `compose_only` lookup (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'pull_policy', 'never') }}`) so swarm does not reject the compose-only extension with \"Additional property pull_policy is not allowed\"."
msgstr "Leidžia žalią `pull_policy:` raktas `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` šabloną. Numatytasis kelias: maršrutas per bendrinį `compose_only` paieška (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'pull_policy', 'never') }}`) taip sūpynės neatmeta tik kompozito- tik plėtinys \"Papildoma savybė pull_policy neleidžiama\"."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `restart:` key in a `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` template. Default path: route through the `compose_restart` lookup so swarm-mode does not silently drop the operator's `docker_restart_policy`."
msgstr "Leidžia žalią `restart:` raktas `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` šabloną. Numatytas kelias: maršrutas per `compose_restart` peržiūrėti taip sūkurinė režimas nėra tyliai nukrenta operatoriaus `docker_restart_policy`."

msgid "Allows a role Dockerfile to pin an exact version inside a `pip install`. The pin normally lives in a `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` under the role's `files/` and is installed with `pip install -r`, so dependabot's `pip` ecosystem can raise it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allows a role other than [web-app-email](../../../../roles/web-app-email/) and its providers to name a concrete mail provider role id. Default path: name `web-app-email`. Reserved for a statement about the provider itself, such as a `required_by` entry for a role the provider includes."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a role task to render a `*.service.j2` itself instead of handing the unit to `sys-service`. Default path: name the template `templates/systemctl.service.j2` and include `sys-service` with `system_service_id`, so the unit also gets the daemon reload, the enable, and the timer, async and flush behaviour. Reserved for units `sys-service` cannot carry, such as a user-scope unit under `$HOME`."
msgstr "Leidžia vaidmenį užduotį padaryti `*.service.j2` pati, o ne perduoti vienetą į `sys-service`. Numatytasis kelias: vardas šabloną `templates/systemctl.service.j2` ir apima `sys-service` su `system_service_id`, todėl riedmenų vienetas taip pat gauna demonon įkelti, įjungti, ir laikmatis, async ir nuleisti elgesį. Rezervuota riedmenų vienetams `sys-service` negali turėti, pavyzdžiui, vartotojo taikymo vienetas pagal `$HOME`."

msgid "Allows a role template, var, default or file to set a log driver other than `journald`: a compose `logging.driver`, a daemon `log-driver` or a `--log-driver` flag. Default path: include `roles/sys-svc-container/templates/logging.yml.j2`, which tags the container with its application and logs to journald, the source the host collector reads. Reserved for a container whose vendor tooling cannot log to journald; the marker MUST name why, and a bare marker is rejected."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a rule in a `roles/*/templates/nftables.conf.j2` fragment to end in an `accept` verdict. Default path: express the intent as a `drop` of what must not pass, or put the rule in the chain carrying the policy it has to overrule, because an `accept` terminates only its own base chain and every other chain at that hook still runs, docker's `drop` policy on forwarded packets included. Reserved for an accept whose only job is to skip the fragment's own later rules."
msgstr "Leidžia taisyklę `roles/*/templates/nftables.conf.j2` fragmentas baigti `accept` verdiktas. Numatytasis kelias: išreikšti ketinimą kaip `drop` tai, kas neturi praeiti, arba įdėti taisyklę į grandinę, vykdant politiką, kurią ji turi viršenybė, nes `accept` nutraukia tik savo bazinės grandinės ir visos kitos grandinės, kad kablys vis dar veikia, doker `drop` politika dėl perduotų paketų įtraukti. Rezervuota priimti, kurio vienintelis darbas yra praleisti fragmentas savo vėliau taisykles."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows a single `when:` item to reference a `run_once_<other>` flag whose suffix differs from the current role."
msgstr "Leidžia single `when:` a punktas `run_once_<other>` žyma, kurios priesaga skiriasi nuo dabartinės funkcijos."

msgid "Allows a task delegated to `localhost` to keep the play's `become`. Default path: set `become: false` on the task or its enclosing block. Reserved for a step that needs root on the controller, such as a mount or a write below `/var/lib/infinito`; the marker MUST name that step. Place it on or directly above the `delegate_to:` line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allows a task to load a Rails application's `db/seeds.rb` through `db:seed`, `db:seed:replant`, `db:setup`, `db:reset` or `db:prepare`. Default path: drop the seed or gate it on `when: DEMO | bool`, because upstream seeds fill a development database and may plant users with a known password. Reserved for seeds verified safe to repeat in production; the marker MUST name why. Place it on or directly above the line where the command value starts (a block scalar's `key: >` line, an inline string, or the first `argv:` item). It never exempts Laravel's default `DatabaseSeeder`, which takes `--class=<Seeder>` instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allows a top-level key in an inventory's `host_vars/**` or `group_vars/**` that no `group_vars`, role `defaults` or role `vars` declares and that the validator does not list as read without a declaration. Default path: move the value to the variable the deploy reads, or delete it. Reserved for a helper the inventory reads itself, such as a domain its own templates interpolate. Place it on or directly above the key's line."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows advanced content filtering (e.g., via Lua body/headers)"
msgstr "Leidžia sudėtingesnį turinio filtravimą (pvz., per Lua kūną / antraštes)"

msgid "Allows an `enabled:` flag that is not a literal `false` on a service whose provider's primary entity carries `lifecycle: eol`, in a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` block, a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` pin under `services:` or `addons:`, or a `roles/*/meta/addons/*.yml` gate whose `bridges:` value names the key, at any depth, because the rule reads an off-shape `bridges` as bound rather than trusting the suppressible `addon-schema` lint to have rejected it. `shared` is deliberately NOT covered: an EOL provider keeps its registration so `disable=` and the preload order keep working. This key is per flag only: the repository-wide scope has its own key `eol-dependency-provider`, so no position inside a file can promote a per-flag marker to it. The policy, including the storage rule and the no-variant-pin rule, lives at [lifecycle.md](../../design/role/services/lifecycle.md). The marker MUST name why the dependency outlives the upstream's end of life; a bare marker is rejected, as with `onion-flag`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows an image reference whose tag names a Debian release by codename. Reserved for an upstream that publishes no numeric tag; the marker MUST name which upstream, because a codename pin can never be raised by the updater."
msgstr "Leidžia atvaizdžio nuorodą, kurios žymių pavadinimai Debian laida pagal kodą. Rezervuota priekiniam žibintui, kuris neskelbia jokių skaitmeninių žymenų; žymeklis PRIVALO nurodyti vardą, kuris turi būti prieš, nes atnaujintojas niekada negali pakelti kablelio."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows an untyped `container inspect` under `roles/`. Default path: pin `--type container`, because a role's overlay network carries the same entity name as its main container, so an untyped inspect can resolve the network and report `map has no entry for key \"State\"`. Use the typed subcommand (`container volume inspect` etc.) when the target genuinely is not a container."
msgstr "Leidžia atspausdinti `container inspect` pagal `roles/`. Numatytasis kelias: prisegti `--type container`, nes vaidmuo 's overlay tinklas atlieka tą patį subjekto pavadinimą kaip ir jos pagrindinis konteineris, todėl untyped patikrinimo gali išspręsti tinklą ir pranešti `map has no entry for key \"State\"`. Naudoti typed pokomandą (`container volume inspect` ir t. t.) kai tikslas iš tikrųjų nėra konteineris."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows contributors on Windows to run the full local stack without a separate VM"
msgstr "Leidžia duomenų teikėjams Windows paleisti visą vietinį kaminą be atskiro VM"

msgid "Allows forced execution during maintenance runs (`CLEANUP`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allows forced execution during maintenance runs (``CLEANUP``)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows instant, low-latency bidirectional traffic"
msgstr "Leidžia greitą, žemą latentinį dvikryptį eismą"

msgid "Allows one reference the [meta/lifecycle.yml](../../../../meta/lifecycle.yml) rule forbids: a role naming a role whose status is `retired`, or a `production` role naming a role beyond production, through a role-id value (`run_after`, `required_by`, `dependencies`, `include_role`/`import_role` `name:`), a quoted role id (`'<role>' in group_names`, `lookup(..., '<role>', ...)`) or a service key it switches on. A role that exists to migrate away from the target belongs in `migrations` in `meta/lifecycle.yml` instead. A marker without a `Reason:` is still reported."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows the agent to resolve unknown APIs and tooling questions without leaving the terminal."
msgstr "Leidžia agentui išspręsti nežinomas API ir įrankinti klausimus nepaliekant terminalo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows the marked `ARG` to carry a default. The caller normally supplies every build argument so a missing one fails the build instead of selecting a base image nobody chose."
msgstr "Leidžia pažymėtą `ARG` atlikti numatytąją. Skambintojas paprastai teikia kiekvieną kūrimo argumentas, todėl trūksta vienas nepavyksta statyti vietoj pasirinkti bazinį vaizdą niekas pasirinko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows the marked `yaml.safe_load` / `safe_dump` call to bypass `utils.cache.yaml`. MUST use `nocheck:`, not `noqa:`."
msgstr "Leidžia pažymėtą `yaml.safe_load` / `safe_dump` iškvietimas apeiti `utils.cache.yaml`. PRIVALO naudoti `nocheck:`, ne `noqa:`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows the marked task to carry a credential without `no_log` on itself or a parent. Marker goes on or directly above the task's `- name:`."
msgstr "Leidžia pažymėtą užduotį atlikti patikinimą be `no_log` pats arba vienas iš tėvų. Žymeklis tęsiasi arba tiesiogiai virš užduoties `- name:`."

msgid "Allows the profile attributes `inetOrgPerson` lacks: `c`, the phonetic names and the time zone"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Allows the redundant `| bool | ternary('true','false')` pattern when a consumer requires the lowercase tokens."
msgstr "Leidžia nereikalingas `| bool | ternary('true','false')` modelis, kai vartotojas reikalauja mažiausių žetonų."

msgid "Allows the secondary address of the `mailbox` email policy; attached to user entries and required by the Keycloak federation only under that policy"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alpine Linux → ``openssh-client``"
msgstr "Alpių Linux → ``openssh-client``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alpine Linux → `openssh-client`"
msgstr "Alpių Linux → `openssh-client`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Also callable directly from Python (unit tests, helpers) without a Jinja context: in that case the only positional argument is the value and compose-style quoting is used."
msgstr "Taip pat skambinama tiesiogiai iš Python (vieneto bandymai, pagalbininkai) be Jinja kontekstas: tokiu atveju vienintelis padėties argumentas yra vertė ir kompozitoriaus stiliaus citavimas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Also manually dispatchable: `cron-images-mirror-all.yml`, `cron-images-cleanup-ci.yml`, `cron-cleanup-stale.yml`, `cron-update.yml`, `cron-release-highest.yml`, `call-release-version.yml`, `call-lint.yml`, `call-test.yml`, `call-test-dns.yml`, `call-test-workspace.yml`, `call-test-runner-smoke.yml`."
msgstr "Taip pat rankiniu būdu siunčiami: `cron-images-mirror-all.yml`, `cron-images-cleanup-ci.yml`, `cron-cleanup-stale.yml`, `cron-update.yml`, `cron-release-highest.yml`, `call-release-version.yml`, `call-lint.yml`, `call-test.yml`, `call-test-dns.yml`, `call-test-workspace.yml`, `call-test-runner-smoke.yml`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alternative"
msgstr "Alternatyvus"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alternative compression style"
msgstr "Alternatyvus suspaudimo stilius"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alternative: Build an inventory where all invokable apps are set as a host variable (as a list)."
msgstr "Alternatyva: Sukurti inventorių, kuriame visos naudojamos programos būtų nustatytos kaip priimančiosios kintamasis (kaip sąrašas)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alternative: Recreate the User"
msgstr "Alternatyvus: Atstatyti User"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alternatively, disable IPv6 only in Docker via `/etc/docker/daemon.json`:"
msgstr "Arba, išjungti IPv6 Tik Docker per `/etc/docker/daemon.json`:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Alternatives weighed 🔀"
msgstr "Pasveriamos alternatyvos 🔀"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always Category-Keyed Maps 🗂️"
msgstr "Visada kategorijos- klaviatūros žemėlapiai 🗂️"

msgid "Always `PUBLIC` and `false`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always create the new domain and user in Mailu first."
msgstr "Visada sukurti naują domeną ir vartotoją Mailu Pirma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always overwrite `image`/`version` from the mirror"
msgstr "Visada perrašyti `image`/`version` nuo veidrodžio"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always purge the Cloudflare cache after significant changes to your website or OpenResty/NGINX configuration."
msgstr "Visada išvalykite Cloudlayler talpyklos po reikšmingų pakeitimų jūsų svetainėje arba OpenResty/ NGINX konfigūracija."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always resolve tokens as: **``users → token store → empty``**"
msgstr "Visada išspręsti žetonus kaip: **``users → token store → empty``**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always resolve tokens as: **`users → token store → empty`**"
msgstr "Visada išspręsti žetonus kaip: **`users → token store → empty`**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Always up-to-date packages; minimal base; fast feedback on upstream changes"
