msgid "By default every Talk stream goes through `web-svc-coturn`, and Janus publishes no port. Set `services.talk.direct_media` to `true` in the inventory to let clients send their media to Janus directly: Janus then announces `networks.internet.ip4` as `nat_1_1_mapping`, takes its media ports from `services.talk.ports.public.relay` (UDP, default 61000-61999) and publishes them on that address, and clients fall back to `web-svc-coturn` only when UDP to that range is blocked. The setting takes effect in compose mode when `web-svc-coturn` provides TURN and `networks.internet.ip4` is an address of the host itself."
