msgid "By default the alias is selectable explicitly but excluded from LiteLLM’s general ``auto`` routing. To opt in, configure the guaranteed capabilities of every model FreeLLMAPI may select, for example:"
msgstr ""

# privilegijuotas `pull_request_target` nustatyti patikrinimus **base merge
# ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) iš bazės saugyklos: PR pakeitimai sujungti į
# bazę, su visais darbo srauto ir pastato-archestracija scenarijus ateina iš
# bazės, niekada iš šakutės. Kadangi `actions/checkout` kitaip atsisako gauti
# PR ref pagal `pull_request_target`, šaltinio kasos rinkiniai
# `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. Nepatikimas pastatas veikia **be
# organizacijos paslapčių** - `secrets: inherit` nėra perduotas ir ji
# patvirtina GHCR su per- darbo `GITHUB_TOKEN` tik todėl piktavališkas šakutė
# negali skaityti saugyklos / organizacijos paslaptis. (4. 4 skyrių).
# `pull_request_target` žetonas vis dar turi `packages: write`, todėl `🛡️
# Trusted` etiketė išlieka tikra pasitikėjimo riba nieko už vaizdo
# paskelbimo.)
msgid "By default — for an **untrusted** fork PR — the privileged `pull_request_target` build checks out the **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) from the base repository: the PR's changes merged onto base, with all workflow and build-orchestration scripts coming from base, never from the fork. Because `actions/checkout` otherwise refuses to fetch a PR ref under `pull_request_target`, the source checkout sets `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. The untrusted build runs **without organization secrets** — `secrets: inherit` is not passed and it authenticates to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` only, so a malicious fork cannot read repository/organization secrets. (The `pull_request_target` token still carries `packages: write`, so the `🛡️ Trusted` label remains the real trust boundary for anything beyond image publication.)"
msgstr ""

