# translated-by: libretranslate
# Lint įrankį ir rodo vieną `ensure()` funkcija. CLI in [_ Pagrindinis _ _ _
# .py](__main__.py) grupės tai užtikrinti skambučius ir taikyti kon-based
# praleisti numatytąjį "all" užpuolimas.
msgid "Each module in this directory owns exactly one lint tool and exposes a single `ensure()` function. The CLI in [__main__.py](__main__.py) groups these ensure calls and applies the stamp-based skip for the default \"all\" invocation."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
# kintamąjį, arba vieną susietąją grupę, išspręstą vienu pagalbos skambučiu.
# Orkestratorius [builder.py](../builder.py) Kartoja registrą [_ _ eiti _ _ _
# eiti](__init__.py) ir paskambina kiekvienam prižiūrėtojui `apply(eb, ctx)`
# kad.
msgid "Each module in this directory owns exactly one variable, or one tightly-coupled group resolved by a single helper call. The orchestrator in [builder.py](../builder.py) iterates the registry in [__init__.py](__init__.py) and calls each handler's `apply(eb, ctx)` in order."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each module owns a private `_reset()` that clears its own cache dicts. The package-level `utils.cache._reset_cache_for_tests()` orchestrates all six (`base`, `applications`, `users`, `domains`, `yaml`, `files`) plus the shared fingerprint memo. Unit tests that exercise the cached paths MUST call it in `setUp` to guarantee clean state across test cases."
msgstr "Kiekvienas modulis turi privatų `_reset()` kad išvalys savo dėklą. Pakuočių lygmuo `utils.cache._reset_cache_for_tests()` orkestrai visi šeši (`base`, `applications`, `users`, `domains`, `yaml`, `files`) pridedamas bendras pirštų atspaudų protokolas. Vieneto bandymai, kurie veikia kasti takai PRIVALO skambinti `setUp` užtikrinti švarią būklę visais bandymo atvejais."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each module, class, or function MUST have exactly one responsibility so that changes to one concern do not ripple into unrelated code."
msgstr "Kiekvienas modulis, klasė, ar funkcija PRIVALO turėti tiksliai vieną atsakomybę, kad pakeitimai į vieną susirūpinimą nėra ripple į nesusijusį kodą."

msgid "Each of them checks the host against the roles the deploy may run on it, so each needs the same three things: that role set, the merged applications the set was derived from, and a reader for one role's rendered config. Building them once keeps the lookups from drifting apart on which roles they check."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each one undoes a shape a translator produced and the source did not ask for. They read the source only to decide whether something was lost, never to change what the translation says."
msgstr "Kiekvienas atima formą vertėjas pagamintas ir šaltinis neprašė. Jie skaityti šaltinį tik nuspręsti, ar kažkas buvo prarasta, niekada pakeisti tai, ką vertimas sako."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each operator workflow has a skill that routes the agent to its authoritative procedure and drives it — clarifying open requirements first, then acting autonomously to completion. Most are `i8-` skills specific to this repository; a few (such as `triage`) are portable skills shared across projects."
msgstr "Kiekvienas operatorius darbo srauto turi įgūdžių, kad maršrutai agentas į jo autoritetingą procedūrą ir vairuoti jį - paaiškinti atvirus reikalavimus pirmiausia, tada veikti savarankiškai iki pabaigos. Dažniausiai `i8-` šiai saugyklai būdingi įgūdžiai; keletas (pvz., `triage`) yra nešiojamieji įgūdžiai, kuriais dalijamasi visuose projektuose."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each override is gated on the resource it needs being present, not on the instance slot: an override whose `:?` guard is unsatisfied would abort the stack outright, so a checkout that was never handed a shared git dir or cache network simply does not layer that file in."
msgstr "Kiekvienas override yra gated dėl išteklių reikia būti, o ne pavyzdžiui lizdas: override `:?` apsauga yra nepatenkintas būtų nutraukti kamino iš karto, todėl kasos, kad niekada buvo įteiktas dalijamasi git Dir ar talpyklos tinklas tiesiog nesluoksnis, kad failas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each persona scenario MUST be named `<persona>: <flow>`, where `<persona>` is the literal token `guest`, `biber`, or `administrator` and `<flow>` is a concise step description (e.g. `dashboard → app → logout`). The persona token MUST appear at the very start of the test title so the Playwright reporter groups runs by persona without further parsing."
msgstr "Kiekvienas persona scenarijus PRIVALO būti pavadintas `<persona>: <flow>`, kur: `<persona>` pažodinis raktas `guest`, `biber`, arba `administrator` ir `<flow>` yra trumpas etapas aprašymas (pvz., `dashboard → app → logout`). Asmeninė simbolis PRIVALO pasirodyti pačioje bandymo pavadinimo pradžioje, kad Playwright reporterių grupės veikia persona be tolesnio svarstymo."

msgid "Each phase merges alone and leaves every target working. Each phase updates the docs and skills its change touches."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each recover mirrors a snapshot with `rsync -aHAX --delete` and first runs the role's backup unit as a rollback point. `--no-safety-backup` skips that (only when the target holds nothing worth saving: fresh host / empty / disposable). `--preview` prints the exact commands without running them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each request becomes a Zammad ticket when `web-app-zammad` is deployed, and always an email to the approvers (the platform administrator's secondary address under the mailbox email policy)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each role declares its licence in ``meta/<role>/license.yml``; the rights of a named licence live once in ``meta/licenses.yml``. The context headings below are derived from those rights, not declared, so a heading can never contradict the matrix under it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each role declares its managed fields in `roles/<role>/meta/forms.yml`, the single point of truth for both the value and the UI mapping. Per form it holds the admin page `path` and its `fields`; per field the `source`, the `mode`, an optional `when` and the input `selector`, and optionally `label`, `type`, `enum`, `validation` and `description`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each role group must contain the default host."
msgstr "Kiekviena pareigų grupė turi turėti numatytąjį kompiuterį."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each role in that closure is then narrowed to the variants that actually reach a seed: variant `i` of a role is kept only when round `i`'s closure — walked on the same variant-merged services maps [the matrix planner](../../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/planner.py) builds its rounds from, and therefore variant-aware at every generation of the chain — contains one of the seeds. A role whose variants do not all qualify enters the whitelist as a `role#0,2` selection token, so an image bump in a provider no longer redeploys the variants that switch that provider off. This applies to every auto-derived whitelist — the weekly update PRs, Dependabot, and any other diff-driven run — because they all resolve through this one path."
msgstr "Kiekvienas vaidmuo, kad uždarymo tada yra susiaurintas variantų, kad iš tikrųjų pasiekti sėklą: variantas `i` vaidmuo yra laikomas tik tada, kai turas `i`'s uždarymo - vaikščiojo ant to paties įvairių susijungusių paslaugų žemėlapiai [matricos planuotojas](../../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/planner.py) kuria savo raundus iš, ir todėl įvairių žino kiekvienos kartos grandinės - yra viena iš sėklų. Vaidmuo, kurio variantai ne visi atitinka baltąjį `role#0,2` atrankos simbolį, todėl vaizdo buferis teikėjas nebedislokuoja variantų, kurie perjungia, kad teikėjas išjungti. Tai taikoma kiekvienam autoišvestis whitelist - savaitės atnaujinimas PRs, Debendabot, ir bet kuris kitas difuzinis paleisti - nes jie visi išspręsti per šį vieną kelią."

msgid "Each role runs the variant :func:`resolve_round` settles on: the clamped round index, the supplied index for a primary app, or the index a `# variant-pin:` in force forces (see :mod:`utils.roles.applications.variant_pins`). Every host of :data:`PRIMARY_ONLY_SERVICE_KEYS` stays on only where a primary app's variant declares it; every other role has it off. Roles without variants are absent from the result so the resolver falls through to its disk-read path."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each role with an ``sso`` service, whether its upstream receives OIDC back-channel logout tokens, and how long its session lives on another network or device when nothing ends it. A link names the version the role pins; a link marked “floating” names the newest tag or branch head read on 2026-11-06, because the role does not pin that component. An application that receives logout tokens declares its own Keycloak client under ``services.sso.oidc.clients``; every other one stays on the shared client."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each role with an `sso` service, whether its upstream receives OIDC back-channel logout tokens, and how long its session lives on another network or device when nothing ends it. A link names the version the role pins; a link marked \"floating\" names the newest tag or branch head read on 2026-11-06, because the role does not pin that component. An application that receives logout tokens declares its own Keycloak client under `services.sso.oidc.clients`; every other one stays on the shared client."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each row recomputes the role's embedded (forward) service deps from that variant's merged ``services`` map, so toggling a sidecar off in a variant drops it from the variant's ``embeds``/``weight``. The consumer (reverse) side is the variant-independent role-level graph: who else in the catalog embeds this role does not change with the role's own variant selection."
msgstr "Kiekvienoje eilutėje recompacts the role 's incorporated (į priekį) paslaugos nutolsta nuo to varianto sujungto ``services`` žemėlapį, taip, togggling šoninės off varianto lašai jį iš varianto ``embeds``/``weight``. Vartotojas (atvirkštinis) pusė yra įvairių nepriklausomų role- lygio diagrama: kas dar kataloge įdeda šį vaidmenį nekeičia su vaidmens savo variantą pasirinkimas."

msgid "Each row was a migration target and now states what its `meta/addons/` declares after the migration. \"Addons\" counts the addon files, \"Required\" those with `required: true`, and \"Bridged services\" are the service keys their `bridges:` lists name, each resolving to a service block of the same role. [test_addons_audit.py](../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_addons_audit.py) classifies every role under `roles/` and fails when a row no longer matches or a role with addons has no row."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each run gets its own copy of ``base`` with the key set to the plan's value, so one run never sees the other's."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each runner instance is provisioned as an ephemeral container using **DooD** (Docker-out-of-Docker — it mounts the host `docker.sock`). Isolation is keyed on the instance number, so parallel jobs never collide:"
msgstr "Kiekvienas bėgikas pavyzdys yra numatytas kaip efemerial konteineris naudojant **DooD** (Docker- out- Docker - ji prideda šeimininką `docker.sock`). Izoliacija yra klavišu ant pavyzdžiui numeris, todėl paraleliniai darbai niekada susiduria:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each scenario MUST live in its own `test-*.js` module (e.g. `test-login-oidc.js`, `test-seaweedfs.js`). `playwright.spec.js` is the thin aggregator that `require()`s every scenario module, keeping each case atomic and individually inspectable. The runner globs every `*.js`, so no extra wiring is needed."
msgstr "Kiekvienas scenarijus PRIVALO gyventi savarankiškai `test-*.js` modulis (pvz., `test-login-oidc.js`, `test-seaweedfs.js`). `playwright.spec.js` yra plonas agregatas, kad `require()`s kiekvieno scenarijaus modulis, kiekvieną atvejį tikrinant pagal atominį scenarijų ir atskirai. Bėgikas žaidžia kas `*.js`, Taigi papildomų laidų nereikia."

msgid "Each scenario is `<id>.yml`:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Each script MUST be entered via `cli.administration.deploy.development exec --env KEY=VAL` (or an equivalent `docker exec -e …` invocation) so the host wrapper can inject the required environment. Each script MUST assert its required env-vars at the top with `: \"${VAR:?}\"` so missing context surfaces immediately. Each script MUST `cd \"${INFINITO_SRC_DIR}\"` before running anything so relative paths resolve against the bind-mounted repo. Each script SHOULD run `./scripts/docker/entry.sh true` for entry bootstrap before the deploy step."
msgstr "Kiekvienas scenarijus PRIVALO būti įrašytas per `cli.administration.deploy.development exec --env KEY=VAL` (arba ekvivalentas `docker exec -e …` užgrobimas) todėl priimančiosios pakuotės gali švirkšti reikiamą aplinką. Kiekvienas scenarijus PRIVALO patvirtinti savo reikalaujamą pavydą viršuje su `: \"${VAR:?}\"` nedelsiant trūksta konteksto paviršių. Kiekvienas scenarijus PRIVALO `cd \"${INFINITO_SRC_DIR}\"` prieš veikia nieko, kad santykiniai keliai išspręsti prieš prikabintas atpirkimo. Kiekvienas scenarijus TURĖTŲ paleisti `./scripts/docker/entry.sh true` įlipimui į butstrapą prieš išlipimo laiptelį."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each service entry lives in the provider role's own `meta/services.yml`, where the file root IS the services map keyed by `<entity_name>` (no `compose:` and no `services:` wrapper). See [layout.md](layout.md) for the full per-role meta layout."
msgstr "Kiekviena paslauga patenka į teikėjo vaidmenį `meta/services.yml`, kur failo šaknis yra paslaugų žemėlapis klaviatūra `<entity_name>` (ne `compose:` ir ne `services:` įvyniojimas)- Matai. [layout.md](layout.md) už visą pe- role meta maketą."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each service in host vars MAY carry a `mirror_policy` field that controls how the override is applied:"
msgstr "Kiekviena tarnyba šeimininko narai GALI turėti `mirror_policy` laukas, kuriame kontroliuojama, kaip taikoma išimtis:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each service-account integration provisions a dedicated non-login identity holding only the upstream permissions the declared allowlist needs. The lookup resolves `mcp.credential.owner`, `source` and `key`; deployment fails when the resolved principal is missing, empty, more privileged than `auth_subject` declares, or shared with an unrelated provider."
msgstr "Kiekvienos tarnybos įrašo integracijos nuostatos speciali ne-prisijungimo tapatybė, turinti tik pirmesnius leidimus deklaruotų leidimų poreikius. Apžvalga išsprendžia `mcp.credential.owner`, `source` ir `key`; dislokavimas nepavyksta, kai išspręstas vykdytojas trūksta, tuščias, labiau privilegijuotas nei `auth_subject` deklaruoja arba dalijasi su nesusijusiu paslaugų teikėju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each settings change MUST be reviewed before it lands. Approval here is equivalent in blast radius to approving a `deny`-rule edit: the next tool call may run under new rules. Operators SHOULD diff the proposed change against the live file before approving and SHOULD decline any change that widens `allowWrite`, removes a `deny` entry, adds a broad `allow` wildcard, or registers a hook command."
msgstr "Kiekvienas nustatymų pakeitimas PRIVALO būti peržiūrėtas prieš jam patenkant. Patvirtinimas čia yra lygiavertis patvirtinimo `deny`-taisyklė redaguoti: kitas įrankis skambutis gali paleisti pagal naujas taisykles. Operatoriai TURĖTŲ atskirti siūlomą pakeitimą nuo gyvų failą prieš patvirtinant ir TURĖTŲ sumažinti bet kokį pakeitimą, kuris išplečia `allowWrite`, pašalina `deny` įrašas, prideda platų `allow` laukinės kortelės, arba registruoja kablys komandą."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Each shim MUST resolve the repository root relative to its own location so it can run from any working directory, MUST forward arguments to the underlying CLI so `--dry-run` and similar flags keep working from the shell, and MUST exit non-zero on CLI failure so the workflow surfaces the error."
msgstr "Kiekvienas shem PRIVALO išspręsti saugyklos šaknis, atsižvelgiant į savo vietą, kad ji gali paleisti iš bet darbo katalogą, PRIVALO siųsti argumentus į pagrindinę CLI taip `--dry-run` ir panašios vėliavos išlaikyti darbą nuo korpuso, ir PRIVALO išeiti non- nulis CLI gedimo, todėl darbo srauto paviršių klaidą."

msgid "Each sign-in method follows ``services.mattermost.login.method.<method>.enabled`` in ``meta/services.yml`` and is rendered into ``templates/env.j2``:"
msgstr ""

