msgid "The bootstrap fallback (`tasks/utils/login_bootstrap_admin.yml`) signs in as the user `meta/users.yml` names, but Keycloak creates that master user only on an empty database, so a master realm keeps the name of its first install: `administrator` before 3c72c2002a (2026-10-08), `keycloakbootstrap` from then on. On an older realm the fallback finds no user, so a refused permanent-admin login without a captured previous password stops the deploy, and the old temporary admin stays with its old password. Options: recover through Keycloak's own `kc.sh bootstrap-admin user` with credentials passed by environment instead of a stored master user, and delete every temporary admin once the permanent admin signs in."
