msgid "The first boot serves nothing until the embedding model is on disk: uvicorn binds only after the lifespan startup, which downloads `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (30 files) from Hugging Face into the data volume. Measured on a slow network (2026-10-14, UTC): container created 08:04:17, `Waiting for application startup` 08:06:27, model loaded 08:14:31, so the proxy answered 502 for eight minutes and the readiness wait of the test stage (08:11:07 to 08:13:47, 30 attempts) failed the deploy. The image healthcheck has no start period, so `sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft` restarted the still downloading container as unhealthy at 08:05:59 and the download began again. Options: embed through the LiteLLM gateway (`RAG_EMBEDDING_ENGINE=openai`) when `litellm` is on, give the service a healthcheck `start_period` that covers the download, or fetch the model in a task before the readiness wait."
msgstr ""

msgid "The first dashboard account is created automatically before the HTTP listener starts, using ``lookup('users', 'platform_administrator').email`` and ``.password``. The role requires a valid email and a password of at least eight characters. Log in with these credentials and add the provider keys you want to use. After the container starts, the role reconciles the single dashboard account through the installed FreeLLMAPI auth service. Redeploys update its email and password to the current platform administrator credentials. Matching credentials cause no account writes; a password change uses the upstream reset operation, which invalidates existing dashboard sessions. Email changes retain the account ID. An installation with multiple dashboard accounts fails instead of selecting an arbitrary account. Provider keys and routing data are preserved."
msgstr ""

