# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Trusted fork PRs: a maintainer-applied *trusted-pr* label runs a fork PR as deliberately released code — the orchestrator skips the fork-prerequisite wait and the privileged *pull_request_target* build switches its source from the base merge ref to the raw PR head, while the built image keeps the merge-SHA tag so every downstream consumer is unchanged. The label is the only switch (applying a label is collaborator-only on GitHub, so fork authors cannot grant it), build-orchestration scripts always come from the base repository, and both unlabeled fork PRs and same-repository PRs are untouched. See [the fork-PR pipeline](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) and [the contributor fork workflow](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."
msgstr "Patikimi šakutės PRs: palaikytojas taikomas *pasitikėjimas- pr* etiketė veikia šakutė PR kaip sąmoningai išleistas kodas - orkestras praleidžia fork-būtina laukti ir privilegijuoti *pull_request_target* stato savo šaltinį nuo pagrindo sujungti ref į neapdoroto PR galvos, o pastatytas vaizdas išlaiko sulie- SHA žymę, todėl kiekvienas pasroviui vartotojas yra nepakitęs. Etiketė yra vienintelis jungiklis (taikant ženklą bendradarbiautojas - tik GitHub, todėl šakutės autoriai negali suteikti), build- orchestration scenarijus visada ateina iš bazinės saugyklos, ir tiek nepažymėtas šakės PRs ir taip pat saugykla PRs yra nepaliesti. Žr. [fork- PR dujotiekis](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) ir [duomenų teikėjo fork darbo srautas](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."

msgid "Trusted measurement sources: the `profile_tasks` timestamp line gives the duration of the previous task, so pair a `TASK` header with the next timestamp line; the `TASKS RECAP` and `Playbook run took` totals; the two per-target wall-clock tables; the pytest summary lines and the `FAILED TARGETS:` line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Trusted sources: the `profile_tasks` timestamp line is the previous task's duration, so a `TASK` header pairs with the next timestamp; the `TASKS RECAP` and `Playbook run took` totals; the two per-target wall-clock tables; the pytest summary and the `FAILED TARGETS:` line. The make exit code is never a verdict, and a quality gate whose test phase is red never runs its lint phase."
