msgid "[served.py](../../../../utils/domains/served.py) resolves the declaration once per play into `CURRENT_PLAY_SERVED_DOMAINS`. Where `wildcard_certificate_available` in [tls_common.py](../../../../utils/tls_common.py) holds for the application, the play serves one name `*.<parent>`; elsewhere it serves `<username>.<parent>` for every inventory user holding the role. A member is served only when `is_member_label` accepts the username. The constructor never fails on a declaration or a member; [served_domains](../../../../plugins/lookup/served_domains.py) also returns the problems, and the declaring role fails on its own. The `tls` and `cert` lookups resolve the served names to their application, the front proxy probes a wildcard name through the host `infinito-probe.<parent>`, and `CURRENT_PLAY_DOMAINS_ALL` carries them into certificates and DNS. `lookup('domains')`, tenancy and `domains.canonical` never contain them, so Keycloak registers no redirect URI for them."
msgstr ""

