msgstr "`INFINITO_DISTRO`, `INFINITO_CONTAINER`, neprivaloma `INSPECT_CMD` arba padėties argonai"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`INFINITO_DNS_HOSTS` can still override the generated list explicitly"
msgstr "`INFINITO_DNS_HOSTS` gali dar aiškiai nepaisyti sukurto sąrašo"

msgid "`INFINITO_DOMAIN`, `INFINITO_SRC_DIR` and `INFINITO_TARGET_KEY` come from the checkout's `.env`, and the address from `INFINITO_TARGET_KEY.address`, which the last reset wrote for this host: the stack address in a compose round, the lab address in a swarm round. A missing `.env` points at `make dotenv`, a missing `.address` at a reset, and a `DOCS_TEST_DOMAIN` other than `INFINITO_DOMAIN` fails the test"
msgstr ""

msgid "`INFINITO_GHCR_MIRROR` decides whether a run uses the mirror. The generated `.env` sets it to `true` on a real GitHub runner and to `false` everywhere else, act included. A non-empty exported value overrides that for one run. [call-test-workspace.yml](../../../../.github/workflows/call-test-workspace.yml) exports `true`, so the workspace suite runs like a local setup and still pulls from GHCR, in its compose drills and, through `make swarm-zombie`, in its swarm drills."
msgstr ""

msgid "`INFINITO_TARGET_IP`, host `.20` of `INFINITO_SUBNET`, derived by [target_ip.py](../../utils/env/handlers/infinito/target_ip.py) so every worktree and runner instance gets its own"
msgstr ""

msgid "`INFINITO_TARGET_KEY` on every holder: the `infinito` container in a compose round, each swarm node in a swarm round. `.pub`, `.known_hosts` and `.address` sit beside it; `.address` is where that holder reaches the target"
msgstr ""

