msgid "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona ir pagrindiniai pareiškimai vyksta besąlygiškai."

