msgid "`agent.yml` holds the machine-readable fields: `runtime`, `lifecycle`, `triggers` (events only), `repositories`, `firewall_roles`, `credentials`, `keepass`, `owner`, `models`, `quotas`, `write_enabled`, `skills`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agent` or `human`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`agent` renders one area with its values. `human` renders the web templates: the chooser for `general`, the area's prompts for every other scope."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agent`: the agent holds the master key itself and works fully autonomously; this mode is set per role in the inventory as an explicit release."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents.max_running` caps the number of agent instances running at once; further starts wait in a queue in trigger order."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/SOUL.md` carries the principles every agent shares, taken from the running agents:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/criteria.yml` maps every criterion to exactly one proof kind and proof; criteria that ask for a probe, a refusal, a time bound or a restart are proven by a scenario"
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/firewall/` is the single source of what an agent may reach. It defines RBAC roles; `agent.yml` binds an agent to roles; the inventory may override bindings and rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/roles/` is the catalog of every employee profile the platform offers. Each profile is usable as a team agent and as a user-started agent."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/roles/counsel/cron.yml` holds one entry, a full run every Monday at 02:00 UTC; a changed dependency manifest or lockfile on the default branch and every agent pull request start a run scoped to that change."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/roles/maintainer/SOUL.md`: skeptical of its own drafts, most of all right before posting; root cause over masking; shortest correct diff; honest residuals; withhold an answer rather than post a plausible wrong one."
msgstr ""

msgid "`agents/routines/` exposes `python -m agents.routines show <routine>` (ordered steps plus Mermaid, for interactive agents) and `python -m agents.routines run <routine>` (autonomous execution)."
