msgstr ""

msgid "`biber` joins the `auditor` role group for its persona journey and opens the central dashboard; `files/playwright/test-rbac.js` proves that biber without a role group is refused. With `sso` disabled Grafana knows only the break-glass account, so `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` is `true` then."
msgstr ""

msgid "`biber` runs in [files/playwright/test-biber-persona.js](./files/playwright/test-biber-persona.js) while `sso` is enabled and is skipped with `SSO_SERVICE_ENABLED=false`, where the only credential left belongs to no user account. The oauth2-proxy admits only the application's administrator RBAC group, so the scenario asserts that `biber` is refused with a 403 at `/oauth2/callback`, stays on that refusal and receives no Postmarks `connect.sid` session."
msgstr ""

msgid "`biber` runs in `files/playwright/test-biber-persona.js` while `sso` is enabled and is skipped with `SSO_SERVICE_ENABLED=false`. Without a Flowise role group, the oauth2-proxy refuses `biber` with a 403 at `/oauth2/callback`, because `sso.oauth2.allowed_groups` in `meta/services.yml` admits only the `administrator` and `mcp` role groups. In the `mcp` role group, `biber` passes the gate and lands on Flowise's own sign-in form: the role grants no Flowise account, so the app shell stays absent and `/api/v1/chatflows` answers 401. The scenario joins `biber` to the group through the Keycloak Admin REST API and removes the membership afterwards."
msgstr ""

