msgid "`tasks/01_setup.yml` \"Realign the administrator password with the declared one\" passes `-e ADMIN_EMAIL=<value> -e ADMIN_PASSWORD=<value>` in the argv of `container exec`: the local full deploy of 2026-10-14 (`MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` off) printed that argv with the administrator password once in its log. Its `changed_when: \"'CHANGED' in ...stdout\"` also matches `UNCHANGED`, so the task reports changed on every run (measured on a role sync with an aligned password). Options: forward both as `-e ADMIN_EMAIL -e ADMIN_PASSWORD` without a value plus the task's `environment:` (pattern: `tasks/02_settings.yml`), and match the whole line (`' CHANGED$'`)."
