msgid "`tasks/02_bench_bootstrap.yml:24-25` and `tasks/02_bench_bootstrap/create_site.yml:20-21` expand `$ADMIN_PASSWORD` and `$DB_ROOT_PASSWORD` into the argument list of `bench` inside the backend container (`set-admin-password \"$ADMIN_PASSWORD\"`, `--admin-password=`, `--db-root-password=`), so both values are part of a process argument list while the command runs (read in the task files, not measured). Cause: the commands receive the secrets as arguments. Options: set the Administrator password through the bench Python interpreter with the value in the environment, the way `files/python/apply/api_bot.py` receives the API bot password, and hand the database root credentials to `bench new-site` through a file or the environment."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_breakglass.yml:20-25` hands the break-glass password to `semaphore user change-by-login` as the `--password` argument of a `container exec` call, so the value is part of the process argument list on the hosting node and in the container while the command runs, and of the command text of the task in a deploy log whenever `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` is off. Cause: the task builds the command line from `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_PASSWORD`. Options: use a stdin or environment route when `semaphore user change-by-login --help` offers one; let a shell inside the container expand `$SEMAPHORE_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, which `templates/env.j2` already sets there, which keeps the value out of the command text of the task but not out of the argument list of the `semaphore` process; or change the password through `POST /api/users/<id>/password` with the JSON body fed on stdin."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_fix-application-schema.yml` \"Back-fill column defaults\" reports `changed` and notifies `compose-up` on every role sync, also when the defaults are already in place; options: let the SQL return the columns it altered and derive `changed_when` from the returned rows."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_install.yml` passes the administrator password to `wp core install` as `--admin_password=<value>` on the command line of `container exec`, where the process list of the host shows it for the run of the command. Options: `wp core install --prompt=admin_password` with the value on stdin, or `wp user update <login> --prompt=user_pass` after an install that sets a throwaway value."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_manager_ops.yml:30` passes `XWIKI_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD` as an argument of `shell/debug_superadmin.sh`, so the secret is in the process list of the stack host and in the deploy log while that task runs. Options: feed it through stdin, hand the script a file path, or let the script read it from the container environment."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_manager_ops.yml` \"copy taiga gateway config\" renders into the cloned `taiga-docker` checkout, which `sys-svc-compose` \"Pull docker repository\" resets on every deploy, so the task reports changed and notifies `compose-up` on every run (measured 2026-10-11 in two consecutive role syncs). Options: render the gateway config outside the checkout and mount it."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_manager_ops.yml` reports \"Realign the administrator password EspoCRM persisted at install\" as changed on every run (`changed_when: rc == 0`), so a second deploy is never idempotent. Options: compare the stored hash first with a PHP check, as `files/php/set_siteurl.php` does for `siteUrl`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_run_one.yml` and `tasks/03_run_pass.yml`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/02_settings.yml:58` renders `OPENPROJECT_RAILS_SETTINGS` including `smtp_password` into the shell command line as `-e OPENPROJECT_RAILS_SETTINGS=<json>`; forward it as `-e OPENPROJECT_RAILS_SETTINGS` plus `environment:`, or feed the JSON on stdin."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/03_administrator.yml` passes the administrator password in argv (`php artisan user:create --password=...`), so it is visible in the process list and in deploy logs with `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` off; Pixelfed's `user:create` has no stdin or file option. Options: pass `-e PIXELFED_ADMIN_PASSWORD` without a value plus the task's `environment:` and run `sh -c 'exec php artisan user:create \"$@\" --password=\"$PIXELFED_ADMIN_PASSWORD\"' sh <other options>` (keeps it out of the host argv and the `-vv` deploy log, pattern: `roles/web-app-erpnext/tasks/02_bench_bootstrap.yml`), or create the account through `php` on stdin with `Artisan::call`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/03_administrator.yml` posted the group member object on every deploy with a body XWiki ignored (`<properties>` wrapper, text outside `<value>`), so an existing installation carries one empty `XWiki.XWikiGroups` object on `XWiki.XWikiAdminGroup` per earlier deploy (measured: two). The post now carries the member and runs once. Options: delete the empty member objects through REST, or leave them (they grant nothing)."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/03_install.yml` passes the database password and the administrator password as positional arguments to `files/install/or_update.sh`, which forwards them in `argv` again (lines 22 `-p\"$DB_PASSWORD\"`, 40 `--dbpass`, 45 `--pass`); the deploy log prints the script line at `-vv`. Options: hand both through the task's `environment:` and `container run -e NAME`, and use `install.php --passfile` for the administrator."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/04_admin.yml <./tasks/04_admin.yml>`__ applies the settings, the administrator and its LDAP link only when the digest of its sources, its inputs and the state OpenProject holds differs from the stamp ``admin-provision.sha256`` in the instance directory. Set ``services.openproject.admin.force`` to ``true`` to run it regardless."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/04_admin.yml:16` passes the administrator password as `-e OPENPROJECT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<value>` in the `argv` of `container exec`, so a `-vv` deploy log prints it and `expand_argument_vars` rewrites a `$NAME` sequence inside it; forward it as `-e OPENPROJECT_ADMIN_PASSWORD` plus the task's `environment:`. The same task reports `changed` on every run; give it a `changed_when` on an output line the script prints only on a real change."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/05_administrator.yml` \"Unblock the administrator username\" reports changed on every deploy (measured 2026-10-11 in the baseline deploy and four consecutive role syncs; the baseline printed \"Unblocked 1 username block(s) for administrator\"), so a username block for the administrator is recreated between runs. Options: find what recreates the block and stop it, or make the unblock idempotent by not recreating it."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/07_reset_admin_password.yml:16` passes `JOOMLA_USER_PASSWORD` as `--password` argument, `tasks/03_install.yml:53` and `:57` expand `J_DB_PASSWORD` and `J_ADMIN_PASSWORD` into `--db-pass=` and `--admin-password=`, and `tasks/05_patch.yml:10` hands the database password to `container exec` as `-e J_DBPASS=`, so each secret is in the process list of the stack host and in the deploy log while its task runs (read from the task files, not measured). Options: feed the values through stdin next to a PHP script, as `tasks/09_design.yml` does with its payload, or through an env file inside the container."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/flavor/ansible/06_proxy_wiring.yml` (line 92) passes `MATRIX_ADMINISTRATOR_PASSWORD` in argv of `register_new_matrix_user -p`, so the `-vv` deploy log prints it whenever `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` is off; options: forward it with `container exec -e NAME` plus the task's `environment:` and read it inside the Synapse container from that variable or from stdin through `--password-file`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/setup/oidc.yml:25` hands the administrator password and `tasks/setup/oidc.yml:30` the Keycloak client secret to `files/php/oidc/client.php` as `-e ADMIN_PASSWORD=…` and `-e OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=…` on the `container exec` command line (read from the role file; `sso` was disabled on the stack of the design pass). Options: send both as a JSON document on stdin after the script, or mount them through `--env-file` with a `0600` file."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/stages/01_constructor.yml` renders once for the bootstrap section, in every deploy mode, right after the `networks` and `service_provider` merges and the `add_host` placements, so the `update` role, the pre-flight checks and the package batch share one render with the `group_names` and `groups` a role sees. Moving it before the placements bakes stale values into the play. The stage-wide task after the token store serves that render while its key still matches, so the carried user records can predate the token store (see the token rule below)."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/stages/02_server.yml` includes the role on every server host, in compose and in swarm, including the NFS and backup hosts; it does nothing while no host of the inventory is in the `web-svc-loki` group. The collector is a node-local compose stack under `/opt/compose/svc-log-collector/`, started with the compose wrapper on each host independently of any swarm stack, so a host outside the swarm ships its journal too."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tasks/utils/` is the repository's home for unnumbered, includable task files, so the entrypoint carries no step number."
msgstr "`tasks/utils/` yra saugyklos namai nenumeruotiems, įskaitant užduočių failus, todėl entypoint atlieka ne žingsnis numeris."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`tasks/utils/mcp/probe.yml`, which hard-fails the deploy when the hub rejects it"
msgstr "`tasks/utils/mcp/probe.yml`, kuris sunkiai-nepavyksta dislokavimo, kai stebulė atmeta jį"

msgid "`tasks/utils/objectfs.yml` copies the plugin from the image into the persistent code volume, runs `admin/cli/upgrade.php`, then writes `MOODLE_OBJECTFS_READY_FILE` into the code volume and purges the caches. `files/build/config.php` names `alternative_file_system_class` only once that file exists, so `install_database.php` and the plugin's own upgrade run on Moodle's default file system. The plugin directory is not usable as that signal: `files/build/moodle-entrypoint.sh` copies the whole image tree into the code volume at container start, before any Ansible task runs."
msgstr ""

msgid "`tasks/utils/validate/providers.yml` validates every declared remote model whose provider has a configured key, after the gateway container starts and before consumers are provisioned. It reads the actual provider key from that container and sends a direct provider request through the installed LiteLLM SDK, without the gateway router or its fallbacks. Missing keys, authentication failures, insufficient credit, denied access, unavailable models and rate limits fail the deploy. Providers without keys and mock models are excluded."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/compose.yml.j2:28` puts `XWIKI_LDAP_BIND_PASS` into `JAVA_OPTS` as a `-D` system property, so it is visible in the process list of the container. Options: write it into `xwiki.cfg` or `xwiki.properties` from the entrypoint, or mount it as a file the configuration reads."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/compose.yml.j2:62` passes `FUNKWHALE_TYPESENSE_API_KEY` as `--api-key` in the `command` of the `typesense` service (compose profile `typesense`, always in swarm), so the key shows in the container argv and in `docker inspect`; options: hand it over as `TYPESENSE_API_KEY` through an env file, or drop the role-local sidecar since `templates/env.j2` wires no `TYPESENSE_*` variable and the api logs \"Typesense is not activated\"."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`templates/compose.yml.j2`: its own standalone stack."
msgstr "`templates/compose.yml.j2`: savo savarankiškai kamino."

msgid "`templates/env.j2:7-10` renders `BRIDGY_APPVIEW_HOST`, `BRIDGY_PLC_HOST`, `BRIDGY_BGS_HOST` and `BRIDGY_PDS_HOST`, while upstream reads `APPVIEW_HOST`, `PLC_HOST`, `BGS_HOST` and `PDS_HOST` (`config.py:116-118`, `hub.py:201-203`), so the rendered values reach no code path (read from both sources, not measured). Options: render the names upstream reads; or drop the four lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/env.j2` lines 33 to 41 set the fixed RabbitMQ login `taiga`/`taiga` and the Erlang cookie `secret-erlang-cookie` for both brokers. Options: generate both through `meta/secrets.yml` and read them in `env.j2`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/env.j2` passes `LDAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, which no script of the LAM 9.7 image reads (`start.sh` reads `LDAP_USER`, `LAM_PASSWORD`, `LDAP_SERVER`, `LDAP_BASE_DN` and friends; the key only feeds the OpenLDAP service of the upstream compose file). It places the LDAP root password into the LAM container environment for nothing, since LAM binds with the password the user types. Option: drop the key."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/env.j2` sets `ESPOCRM_CONFIG_DEFAULT_CURRENCY` to the host currency (measured `EUR`) while `currencyList` and `baseCurrency` stay at the upstream `USD`, so `POST api/v1/Opportunity` with the default currency fails with `Field validation failure; entityType: Opportunity, field: amount, type: validCurrency`. Options: also set `ESPOCRM_CONFIG_CURRENCY_LIST` and `ESPOCRM_CONFIG_BASE_CURRENCY` to the host currency, or keep the upstream default currency."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/janus.jcfg.j2`, mounted as a config at `/usr/local/etc/janus/janus.jcfg`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/javascript.js.j2:4` sends every page whose visible text contains \"your Pi-hole\" to `/admin/`. With `services.javascript` enabled the Clients page (`/admin/groups/clients`), the Pi-hole diagnosis page (`/admin/messages`) and the Teleporter settings (`/admin/settings/teleporter`) therefore open the dashboard instead of their own content (measured on the compose stack with `javascript` on and `sso` off: the browser ends on `/admin/` and shows the dashboard tiles; the templates of all three pages carry the phrase in their help texts). Cause: `redirectIfAccessDenied` matches a phrase of the 403 page that upstream also uses on regular pages. Options: match the 403 page by its own markup (`h2.error-headline`, body class `page-error403`) instead of by a phrase; return early when `document.body.classList.contains(\"logged-in\")`; or drop the redirect, because the app answers `/` with its own 308 to `/admin/` once the request host equals `webserver.domain`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`templates/javascript.js.j2` inserts the \"SSO with ...\" link into the sign-in form whenever the form shows, also with `services.sso.enabled` false, where no `MM_GITLABSETTINGS_*` is rendered (measured on the compose stack with `sso` off: `a[href='/oauth/gitlab/login']` is present on `/login`). Options: render the snippet only under `MATTERMOST_OIDC_ENABLED`."
msgstr ""

